  "step_2": "The individual considers the potential gain of 1000 Euros more in Lottery A compared to Lottery B. They emphasize that this additional 1000 Euros makes a 'big difference' and justify their choice by stating they were willing to give up a 5% higher chance of winning (25% in B vs. 20% in A) in order to have the chance to win 1000 Euros more. The individual focuses on the absolute difference in the maximum payout (4000 vs. 3000) and the trade-off between probability (5% lower chance) and the larger prize. They do not mention risk, uncertainty, or variability in outcomes in terms of statistical dispersion or variance.",
