  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and preferring the lottery with higher variance. The individual did not mention variance, nor did they refer to the spread of outcomes or risk in statistical terms. Instead, their justification is based on the perceived insignificance of the probability difference and the appeal of the higher monetary prize. While the individual’s choice aligns with the decision reason (they chose Lottery A, which has higher variance), their reasoning does not reflect an evaluation of variance. They focus on the relative size of the prize and the subjective insignificance of the probability gap, not on the statistical dispersion of outcomes. Therefore, although the outcome matches, the underlying rationale does not match the decision reason. The individual did not use the variance-based rule to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
